From 8feb5710bb0f84574d8c9854fad1e01a032116b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:39:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Group the solver options into validated dataclasses

equicdft.solver.options defines ConvergenceOptions, EulerOptions (with an
optional AndersonOptions), MinimizeOptions, Constraints and Initialization,
frozen dataclasses that validate their fields once with the ranges the
solver used to check inline. GridSolver.solve takes the groups by keyword
and still accepts every flat keyword (max_iter=, mixing=, anderson=True
with anderson_history=, particle_numbers=, initial_rho=, ...);
resolve_options merges the two forms and rejects a field given both ways
and unknown keywords. The scalar and fixed-dipole entry points read their
settings from the groups, so the ~120 duplicated validation lines are gone.
One behavior change: options of the method that is not selected are
validated too (they used to be ignored). Golden outputs unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
