From 205f89b27049d920d12f5f5aa0920d542ab53e25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:43:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Move the scalar Euler and minimize drivers into their own
 modules

solver/euler.py (solve_euler) and solver/minimize.py (minimize_density)
hold the two iteration drivers as functions of the solver, the prepared
fields and their option groups; GridSolver.solve keeps the problem setup,
dispatch and result assembly. Bodies are unchanged apart from reading the
option fields, so the golden outputs are identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
