From 24f4314b09ecd1209bd91a8dcf483d510e38178b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:08:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Move the fixed-dipole solver into its own module and
 align the result conventions

solver/dipoles.py holds the coupled (rho, P) evaluation, bounds, Euler and
minimize drivers as functions of the solver (bodies unchanged, including
their enable_grad decorators); solver/results.py holds the result-key
aliases; the accessibility-mask helper joins numerics. GridSolver.solve is
now problem setup, dispatch and result assembly only. The fallback of the
plan applies deliberately: the coupled drivers use a different mirror map,
acceptance test and residual bookkeeping than the scalar ones, so folding
them into one loop would either change numbers or leave the loop as a thin
skeleton; instead both families share the option groups, the constraint
helpers and now the result conventions. Scalar results gain the coupled
path's `status` ("converged", "max_iter", "line_search_failed", "stalled")
and `maximum_residual` / `rms_residual` entries (equal to the density
residuals). Goldens re-recorded for the two added keys; every previously
recorded value is unchanged.

